so which of your friends and family  freaked out the most when you told them  that you got cast in a steven spielberg  movie called west side story  i think  i think my mom just freaked out because  my mom is a big theater fan um  um she did theater in in back in cuba  when she lived there and she was just  this was like a dream come true that you  know i was able to almost do what she  wanted to do so she was so excited about  it and so  it was just unbelievable yeah yeah my  mom  my mom was a little like you did what  oh my god  yeah it was a very funny moment she's  and my mother is a woman of few words  so  it was uh it was pretty great  uh like both of you and the planet i am  a huge steven spielberg fan and i am  curious you know did you have any  expectations going in of what it would  be like to work with him and did those  expectations get sort of achieved or  what surprised you about working with  him  well i i don't know about you but i  watched the the spielberg documentary i  believe it was on amazon prime at the  time and i  thought i was going to walk in  uh to an experience with the director  who was going to tell me exactly what he  wanted and how he wanted it and so i  just assumed i was like great i'm going  to be ready for him to  be very very clear and i'm going to  deliver  and then  i got there and it was the complete  opposite  he was sort of like  no i hired you because i trust you amita  is yours and run wild  and there was not a moment that he  wasn't asked he wasn't paying attention  or asking me he was like did that feel  good for you did that feel authentic  some does that feel off  do we want to try something different he  was constantly curious and constantly  asking me questions wanted to make sure  that that it was in line with  not only my understanding of the  character but my understanding of my  lived experience um because he was very  interested in allowing our lived  experiences to inform these characters  and it was just incredibly collaborative  so  uh my expectation was totally shattered  because i got an even better version of  spielberg than i  anticipated  no i feel exactly the same way i went in  thinking that i was just gonna be this  puppet and i was ready to you know just  oh you want me to stand there i'll stand  there you want me to oh here my hand  here okay you know i was i was expecting  that and then i go in and like you said  he's just like  just you do you do whatever you want to  do  and it's scary because it's a huge  response  responsibility he's giving all this  trust over to you  and i you know i'm just kind of blown  away that he trusts me that much um  and yeah so it completely shattered my  expectations and in the end i think it  benefits us as artists because he forces  you to believe in yourself he forces you  to be strong and to be confident and to  go out there and show  what you can do you know he's not there  to tell you what to do he's there to  push you to do what you want to do so  that was incredible yeah  i don't think enough people realize what  it really takes to make a movie on this  scale and scope the behind the scenes  the pre-production the production the  post-production the list goes on and on  and the musical numbers forget it so  what do you wish more people knew  about making like a musical on this size  you know  i think you you literally hit the nail  on the head  the general public doesn't realize how  how hard it is to get not only get a  movie like this made but there are  countless people involved in this  process like hundreds of jobs  are given to people so that we can make  this movie and it's it's not just the  work of one man it's the work of  many many many people hundreds of  incredible and so much you know  blood sweat tears effort  yeah  emphasis on tears goes into making this  movie a reality um  i don't think people realize that in  general about movie making but  specifically epic films like this one  um  you know  it's a work of art it's it's very  carefully crafted um  and there's so much attention to every  little detail in this um and nothing  nothing is there for no reason  everything is there for a very specific  reason um and that's just how stephen  works yeah um and yeah just a commitment  to detail especially when you take on a  cultural project like this  um and i have to say our team was very  sensitive to  our culture and they brought in experts  and they went to groups of people who  potentially did not agree with them and  actively wanted to know what their  grievances were so that they could try  and correct them and that is something  we don't see in the entertainment  industry happen every day and i think  it's an example of how we can and should  be moving forward  i completely agree i really want to  commend both of you on your performances  you guys did such great work thank you  so much for your time so much thank you  so much thank you
 

